    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Onformative is a Berlin studio for generative art, design, and creative technology, founded in 2010 by Julia Laub (co-founder, managing director) and Cedric Kiefer (co-founder, creative lead). Both founders have 15+ years building at the intersection of code, art, and brand communication. Clients include Nike, Samsung, Porsche, IBM, AT&T, Klarna, and OPPO; work spans data-driven installations, AI-augmented artworks, generative brand systems, and spatial interventions. The studio self-describes as a small, experienced core team with flat hierarchies; the 2-10 size is plausible given the lean studio model and financial filings, though exact headcount is not public. Autonomy set to 4: director-level founders with deep specialist practice, but this is a studio entry not an individual. Work Status: Studio (the entity is the studio itself). Capabilities currently tagged as Frontend development (web) appears to be a migration bulk default and likely does not reflect the studio's actual practice; open question filed.",
